{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>For I will not forsake you.</b> And this that I have said — that after the greater part of the exile you shall break forth on every side and not perish in the distresses of exile — shall come to pass because during the days of the exile I will not forsake you, as it says: וְאַף גַּם זֹאת בִּהְיוֹתָם בְּאֶרֶץ אוֹיְבֵיהֶם לֹא מְאַסְתִּים וְלֹא גְעַלְתִּים לְכַלֹּתָם לְהָפֵר בְּרִיתִי אִתָּם (Leviticus 26:44)." "<b>Until I have done.</b> While I have not yet done what I have now declared to you in saying <b>and you shall spread out</b>, for the word עַד sometimes conveys the sense of 'while not yet,' as in עַד שֶׁהַמֶּלֶךְ בִּמְסִבּוֹ (Song of Songs 1:12), עַד לֹא עָשָׂה אֶרֶץ וְחוּצוֹת (Proverbs 8:26). Yet after this great deliverance is accomplished, He will not only show kindness to His people by not forsaking them, but will increase His kindness upon them to walk among them, as it says: וְהִתְהַלַּכְתִּי בְּתוֹכְכֶם (Leviticus 26:12)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:14.546521369Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}